    <back>
      <floats-group id="article-34402.s17">
        <fig id="article-34402.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Necrotizing Gingivitis with Pseudomembrane Formation. The image shows necrotic interdental papillae covered by a grayish pseudomembrane, characteristic of early-stage necrotizing periodontal disease. Contributed by Dr. Mohan M. Muthal, CC BY-SA 4.0 (https///creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0), via Wikimedia Commons</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="NG" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-34402.s18">
        <fig id="article-34402.image.f2" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Necrotizing Gingivitis. The image shows a grayish-white pseudomembrane over necrotic gingiva with loss of interdental papillae. Contributed by Dr.Mohamed HAMZE, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="NG__2" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-34402.s19">
        <fig id="article-34402.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Noma. Also known as <italic toggle="yes">cancrum oris</italic> or mouth gangrene, this condition involves rapidly progressing gangrenous destruction of orofacial tissues, often beginning as necrotizing stomatitis. Contributed By Brian L. Fisher, California Academy of Sciences. - Tonna JE, Lewin MR, Mensh B (2010) A Case and Review of Noma. PLoS Negl Trop Dis 4(12): e869. doi:10.1371/journal.pntd.0000869 (direct link to the image), CC BY 2.5, https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=12651196</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Noma_xcancrum_orisx_case_xPLoSx" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
